## FRONTEND UX FIXES APPLIED (v1.3.4)

All these bugs are FIXED — do not revert:

1. **Blank screen (never showed result)**: `startListening()` returned a Promise that
   hung when `stopListening()` called Voice.stop() but never resolved it.
   Fix: `ListenSession` struct + idempotent `settle()` helper in useSpeech.ts.

2. **TTS Android race**: `Speech.stop()` + `Speech.speak()` same tick — previous
   utterance's `onStopped` called `setIsSpeaking(false)` on new utterance.
   Fix: utterance-ID counter; 300ms Android delay (was 50ms — too short); 3900 char cap; watchdog timer.

3. **WebSocket silent drop**: `sendQuery` returned void, discarded queries when
   socket was closed.
   Fix: `pendingQueryRef` queues one query when disconnected; flushes on ws.onopen;
   `sendQuery` returns boolean.

4. **Processing forever (no escape)**: `startProcessingTimer()` was never called
   from the `handleMicPress` path — no 30s timeout to break out of Processing state.
   Fix: `startProcessingTimer()` called before `sendQuery()` in handleMicPress.

5. **AsyncStorage overwrite**: Loading history from AsyncStorage overwrote live
   in-session messages.
   Fix: functional updater guard: `prev.length === 0 ? parsed.slice(-20) : prev`.

6. **Settings screen showing server URL**: utilsnow.com must not be visible to
   colleagues who share the app.
   Fix: SettingsScreen v1.3.3 shows only Wake Word Active status + About card.

7. **BLACK SCREEN during voice processing (v1.3.4)**: Android's WindowManager renders
   `android:windowBackground` before React Native JS thread repaints during every
   activity transition (STT overlay dismiss triggers onPause → onResume on MainActivity).
   Fix A (native): styles.xml windowBackground → `@android:color/transparent` so no
     color is ever shown during transitions.
   Fix B (JS safety net): VoiceScreen fadeAnim initializes to 1; AppState 'active'
     listener calls `fadeAnim.setValue(1)` to recover from any RN animation edge case.

8. **TTS silent on Android (v1.3.4)**: Voice (STT) held Android audio focus after
   `onSpeechResults` fired. expo-speech tried to acquire focus 50ms later but STT hadn't
   released it yet → TTS silently dropped.
   Fix: `settle()` calls `Voice.stop()` before resolving; delay increased to 300ms.

9. **Permission dialog causing extra onPause/onResume (v1.3.4)**: `PermissionsAndroid.request()`
   was called on every mic press. On first use it shows a system dialog → triggers
   MainActivity onPause → onResume → potential windowBackground flash (amplifies bug #7).
   Fix: cache permission result in ref; use `check()` first, `request()` only if denied.

10. **Wake word _taskRunning global (v1.3.4)**: Module-level `_taskRunning` was shared
    across background service restarts (`restartOnTaskRemoved: true`), causing audio
    capture to stop mid-session when the service restarted.
    Fix: moved to per-invocation local variable inside `wakeWordTask`.

11. **USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT (v1.3.4)**: Declared in manifest but never used;
    on Android 14+ this caused degraded notification behavior / visual disruption.
    Fix: removed from AndroidManifest.xml.

## WAKE WORD SETUP

Sherpa-ONNX KWS (Apache 2.0) — no account, no key, no expiry.
Model: sherpa-onnx-kws-zipformer-gigaspeech-3.3M (~5 MB int8)
Keywords: `▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35` and `▁HE Y ▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35`
Assets in APK: frontend/android/app/src/main/assets/jarvis_kws/
Runtime copy: expo-file-system.copyAsync(asset:// → documentDirectory/sherpa_kws/)
Audio capture: react-native-audio-record at 16kHz/mono/Int16 → Float32 → KWS.acceptWaveform()

Setup:
1. Install APK from https://utilsnow.com/jarvis/app.apk
2. Open app → Settings → toggle "Wake word" ON
3. Grant microphone permission
4. Say "Hey Jarvis" → app opens Voice screen and starts listening

