## SAMPLE QUERIES AND EXPECTED RESPONSES

Q: "What meetings do I have today?"
A: Spoken natural English summary of today's schedule (or "no meetings today")

Q: "What are my overdue action items?"
A: Lists overdue items with priority and due dates

Q: "Am I free tomorrow afternoon?"
A: Checks calendar for conflicts in that time window

Q: "What did we discuss in the Q4 review?"
A: Semantic search over meeting chunks — returns CFO discussion summary

Q: "Check my inbox"
A: "You have no unread emails" (stub in mock mode; live with Graph API)

Q: "What time is the 1:1 with Bharath?"
A: "Your next 1:1 with Bharath is at 6:30 AM on Tuesday, October 11"

## VERSION HISTORY

v1.3.5 (2026-10-10):
  - "Tap microphone and try again" bug FIXED (root cause: Voice.destroy() missing).
    @react-native-voice/voice requires destroy() before each start() on Android to reset
    native module state. After onSpeechResults, Voice enters "stopped-but-not-destroyed"
    state that rejects subsequent start(). Fix: destroy() + re-bind handlers at session start.
  - Removed Voice.stop() from settle() — Voice auto-stops after onSpeechResults; calling
    stop() again corrupts state. 300ms TTS delay provides sufficient audio focus gap.
  - Silence auto-stop feature: If user speaks then pauses 2s with no new partial results,
    listening automatically ends. Eliminates need for manual stop button. Timer resets on
    each partial result (new spoken word).
  - Verified: 12/12 rapid-fire queries passing (includes tests 2-12 which fail with old bug).

v1.3.4 (2026-10-10):
  - BLACK SCREEN FIX (root cause): styles.xml windowBackground → @android:color/transparent
    (was @color/activityBackground = #0A0A0A) so Android WindowManager shows nothing during
    activity transitions (STT overlay dismiss, permission dialogs).
  - BLACK SCREEN FIX (safety net): VoiceScreen.tsx fadeAnim starts at 1 (not 0); AppState
    listener forces opacity=1 on every app → active transition (covers all Android onResume paths).
  - TTS SILENT FIX: settle() now calls Voice.stop() before resolving; this releases Android
    audio focus so expo-speech can acquire it. Previously TTS was silently blocked.
  - TTS TIMING FIX: Android TTS delay increased 50ms → 300ms (STT audio session needs time
    to fully close before TTS can acquire audio focus).
  - PERMISSION FIX: requestMicPermission() now caches result; uses check() before request()
    so system dialog never shows on 2nd+ mic press (avoids extra onPause/onResume cycle).
  - WAKE WORD FIX: _taskRunning moved from module-level global into wakeWordTask local scope;
    prevents shared state corruption across background service restarts.
  - MANIFEST FIX: Removed USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT (declared but never used; caused Android
    14+ notification degradation).
  - TYPESCRIPT FIX: MicButton.tsx Easing.sine → Easing.sin (pre-existing typo, now clean).
  - 8/8 queries verified passing at 1.0–4.8s after APK rebuild.

v1.3.3 (2026-10-10):
  - LLM switched to Groq (openai/gpt-oss-120b, 1000 RPM, no daily limit)
  - _make_llm() factory: Groq → Gemini → heuristic-only fallback chain
  - langchain-openai added to requirements.txt
  - Settings screen: URL completely removed from UI (v1.3.3)
  - Health endpoint exposes llm_provider + llm_model
  - 8/8 queries verified passing at 0.9–3.5s

v1.3.0 (2026-10-10):
  - Blank screen fix: ListenSession + settle() in useSpeech.ts
  - TTS race fix: utterance-ID guard + 50ms Android delay
  - WebSocket queue fix: pendingQueryRef, returns boolean, flush on reconnect
  - Processing-forever fix: startProcessingTimer() before sendQuery()
  - AsyncStorage overwrite fix: functional updater guard
  - Browser test UI at /test endpoint
  - Graph API tools: availability_agent, email_agent
  - MS Entra ID integration design complete

v1.1.0 (2026-10-10):
